-- title:
--   Smooth-point stalks at every layer from the base layer
-- statement:
--   The setting is fixed by the following data. A prime $q$ with $5 \le q$; a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A`, with `hW` saying that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: those places $w$ which are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen _ M')` lies in `ssJSet q`. A chosen member $s$ of $W$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field into the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the unit-group reduction map given by `dvd_sq_mul q M'`. Further, a constant-reduction datum $R_0$ of type `ConstantReduction A ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the generic-fibre field together with a surjective residue map onto the special field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$, and a degree-preserving map on places compatible with divisors of functions), subject to `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image `coeffMap A.subtype y` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction `coeffMap (IsLocalRing.residue ↥A) y`.
--
--   The base-field hypotheses concern an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$: writing $A \cap k_0$ for the contraction `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, it is assumed that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), that it is a henselian local ring (`hhens`), that its residue field is algebraically closed (`hres`), and (`hκ`) that every $a \in A$ differs from some $c \in k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   The auxiliary arithmetic data are: a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   The layer data are: a type $\iota$, a family $K : \iota \to$ intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with each $K\,n$ finite over $k_0$ (`hKfin`), valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K\,n$ which are the contractions of $A$ (`hAn`: $x \in A_n \iff x \in A$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$); and the base layer: an intermediate field $K_b$ with `hKb : Kb = ⊥`, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ which is the contraction of $A$ (`hAb`), and an element $\varpi_b \in A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$ (`hϖb`) and non-zero (`hϖb0`).
--
--   The conclusion is stated for `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. It asserts: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that the compositum of the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $F_0$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`, and such that the linear-disjointness clause holds (for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of the image of $K'$ with $F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$), and for every field `FSS` which is an algebra over `ResidueField ↥A`, every regular prolongation $R$ of type `RegularProlongation A ↥(fieldBar q M') FSS` (a valuation subring `R.integers` with surjective residue map onto `FSS` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$, and satisfying the scaling clause `exists_smul_mem`) such that an element of $F_0$ lies in `R.integers` precisely when it lies in $W_0$: the base-layer package implies the all-layer package, both described next.
--
--   Both halves of the implication open with the same Drinfeld identification clause: for every algebra structure of `GaloisField q 2` on `ResidueField ↥A`, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField ↥A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), there exist a subgroup `Cs` of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of `GaloisField q 2` and an isomorphism $e$ of `ResidueField ↥A`-algebras from `FSS` onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q (ResidueField ↥A) Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field of the subgroup generated by the actions of the elements of `Cs`, such that `Nat.card Cs = 2 * placeWidthChar q M' s` (with `placeWidthChar` the quotient of `jWidthChar q` of the $j$-value of the place by its $j$-ramification), and such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ for which `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves `R.integers` and for which $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the map $e$ carries the action of `R.resAut (levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹)` on `FSS` to [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction q (ResidueField ↥A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$.
--
--   The base-layer package (hypothesis of the implication) asserts, besides that clause, the existence of a finite set $N$ of places of `FSS` over `ResidueField ↥A`, of subrings $S_b\,Q$ of `fieldBar q M'`, of ring homomorphisms $\varphi_b\,Q : A_b[X] \to S_b\,Q$ and $\chi_b\,Q : S_b\,Q \to$ `ResidueField ↥A`, and of sets $D_b\,Q$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that: $|N| = q+1$; there is a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` contained in `R.integers`, contained in $S_b\,Q$ for every $Q \notin N$, and such that every $z \in$ `FSS` lying in the valuation subring of every $Q \notin N$ is the residue of some element of $B$; and for every $Q \notin N$: the image of $A_b$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $S_b\,Q$; $\varphi_b\,Q$ sends the constant $a$ to that image; $\chi_b\,Q(\varphi_b\,Q(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in `ResidueField ↥A`; $\chi_b\,Q(\varphi_b\,Q(X)) = 0$; $S_b\,Q$ is a local ring with $\ker \chi_b\,Q$ its maximal ideal; $S_b\,Q$ is contained in the compositum of the image of $K_b$ with $F_0$, and every element of that compositum is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in S_b\,Q$, $h \ne 0$; $\varphi_b\,Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; $S_b\,Q \subseteq$ `R.integers` and an element of $S_b\,Q$ lies in the maximal ideal of `R.integers` precisely when it is divisible by $\varphi_b\,Q(C\,\varpi_b)$; every $f \in S_b\,Q$ lies in `R.integers`, its residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there is the image of $\chi_b\,Q\,f$ under `ResidueField ↥A` $\to$ `Q.ResidueField`; the residue of $\varphi_b\,Q(X)$ has $Q$-order $1$; and $D_b\,Q$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ such that every $f \in S_b\,Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$, and such that $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is $< 1$ precisely when $\chi_b\,Q\,f = 0$. Finally, the discs separate the places off $N$ (if $P \in D_b\,Q \cap D_b\,Q'$ with $Q, Q' \notin N$ then $Q = Q'$), for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_b\,Q$ the $P$-order of the element $j$ of `fieldBar q M'` (the image of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` under `hle`) is non-negative, and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves `R.integers`: membership of $Q$ in $N$ is invariant under `R.resAut τ`, and for $Q \notin N$ one has `smulDisc τ (Db Q) = Db (R.resAut τ • Q)`.
--
--   The all-layer package (conclusion of the implication) asserts the same Drinfeld identification clause together with the existence of a finite set $N$ of places of `FSS` over `ResidueField ↥A`, of subrings $S_n\,Q\,n$ of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by places and by $\iota$, of ring homomorphisms $\varphi_n\,Q\,n : A_n[X] \to S_n\,Q\,n$ and $\chi_n\,Q\,n : S_n\,Q\,n \to$ `ResidueField ↥A`, and of sets $D_n\,Q\,n$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that:
--
--   (i) $|N| = q+1$.
--
--   (ii) There is a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` contained in `R.integers`, contained in $S_n\,Q\,n$ for every $Q \notin N$ and every $n$, and such that every $z \in$ `FSS` lying in the valuation subring of every $Q \notin N$ is the residue of some element of $B$.
--
--   (iii) For every $Q \notin N$ and every $n \in \iota$: the reduction map $A_n \to$ `ResidueField ↥A` is surjective; the image of $A_n$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $S_n\,Q\,n$; $\varphi_n\,Q\,n$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_n\,Q\,n(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$; $\chi_n\,Q\,n(\varphi_n\,Q\,n(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$; $\chi_n\,Q\,n(\varphi_n\,Q\,n(X)) = 0$; for every $c \in A_n$ with zero residue there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n\,Q\,n \to A_n$ splitting $\varphi_n\,Q\,n \circ C$, inducing $\chi_n\,Q\,n$ on residues, and sending $\varphi_n\,Q\,n(X)$ to $c$; every $f \in S_n\,Q\,n$ lies in `R.integers` with residue in the valuation subring of $Q$, whose residue there is the image of $\chi_n\,Q\,n\,f$; the residue of $\varphi_n\,Q\,n(X)$ has $Q$-order $1$; $D_n\,Q\,n$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ such that every $f \in S_n\,Q\,n$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$, and $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f < 1$ precisely when $\chi_n\,Q\,n\,f = 0$; $\varphi_n\,Q\,n(X) \ne \varphi_n\,Q\,n(C\,c)$ for all $c \in A_n$; $S_n\,Q\,n$ is a local ring whose maximal ideal is the zero set of $\chi_n\,Q\,n$, and is Noetherian and a unique factorisation monoid; $S_n\,Q\,n$ is contained in the compositum of the image of $K\,n$ with $F_0$, and every element of that compositum is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in S_n\,Q\,n$, $h \ne 0$; the linear-disjointness clause holds at the layer $K\,n$ (families $c$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K\,n$ admit no non-trivial relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ with coefficients $a_i$ in that compositum); for every ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n\,Q\,n \to A_n$ splitting $\varphi_n\,Q\,n \circ C$ and inducing $\chi_n\,Q\,n$ on residues, $\ker \chi$ is generated by $\varphi_n\,Q\,n(X) - \varphi_n\,Q\,n(C(\chi(\varphi_n\,Q\,n(X))))$; there is a generator $\varpi$ of the maximal ideal of $A_n$, non-zero, such that $\varphi_n\,Q\,n(C\,\varpi)$ is prime, such that an element $f$ of the compositum lies in `R.integers` precisely when $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in S_n\,Q\,n$ and $\varphi_n\,Q\,n(C\,\varpi) \nmid h$, and such that for every prime $p$ of $S_n\,Q\,n$ not associated to $\varphi_n\,Q\,n(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x \in S_n\,Q\,n$ there is a monic $r \in A_n[X]$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of the image of $r$ under $\varphi_n\,Q\,n \circ C$; and there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_n\,Q\,n$ such that every $f \in S_n\,Q\,n$ can be written $f = g/h$ with $g$ and $h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$, and $h$ the image of a unit of $S_n\,Q\,n$.
--
--   (iv) For every $Q \notin N$ the layers are compatible: there is a monotonicity witness, for $K\,n \le K\,n'$, of $S_n\,Q\,n \subseteq S_n\,Q\,n'$, such that for $K\,n \le K\,n'$ the ring $S_n\,Q\,n'$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_n\,Q\,n$ together with the image of $A_{n'}$; the elements $\varphi_n\,Q\,n(X)$ have the same image in `fieldBar q M'` for all $n, n'$; and for $K\,n \le K\,n'$ the map $\chi_n\,Q\,n'$ restricts to $\chi_n\,Q\,n$ on $S_n\,Q\,n$.
--
--   (v) For $Q, Q' \notin N$ and each $n$, a place $P$ lying in both $D_n\,Q\,n$ and $D_n\,Q'\,n$ forces $Q = Q'$.
--
--   (vi) For $Q \notin N$, every $n$ and every $P \in D_n\,Q\,n$, the $P$-order of the element $j$ of `fieldBar q M'` (the image under `hle` of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq`) is non-negative.
--
--   (vii) For every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, preserving `R.integers`, and every place $Q$: membership in $N$ is invariant under the induced automorphism `R.resAut τ`, and for $Q \notin N$ and every $n$ one has `smulDisc τ (Dn Q n) = Dn (R.resAut τ • Q) n`.
--
--   This is the functorial step in the analysis of the supersingular column of the modular curve at level $q^2M'$: it propagates the smooth-point stalk data (étale charts $A_n[X] \to S_{Q,n}$ with their residue discs, the affine chart $B$, and the Drinfeld identification of the special fibre) from the base layer $k_0$ to every finite layer $K\,n$, with the transition compatibilities between layers, for each admissible pair $(F_0, W_0)$ and each regular prolongation $R$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_affineChart), which assembles the supersingular local data at level divisible by $q^2$.
